  "body": "Follow-up to #287 (first slice: PR #382, a read-only Machines pane with browse and validate).\n\n**Wanted:** the Machines pane creates and edits machine files.\n- **New from template:** copy a listed machine. **New blank:** start from the required keys for a kind.\n- **Edit as a property grid:** collapsible groups (axes and travels, rotaries and limits, spindle range, feeds, tool changer and stations, coolant codes, live-tool codes, units), with tooltips naming each key.\n- **Save / Save As** writes to the user machines folder. Shipped files stay read-only. The folder follows the decision on #287: a `CAMCRAFT_MACHINES` override, otherwise `<platform data dir>/camcraft/machines`; resolution lives in the app layer.\n- **`machine::validate`** (from PR #382) runs before saving. Each refusal is shown on its field and blocks the save, so a file is never half-written (write to a temp file, then rename).\n- **Unknown keys** in a hand-written `.mch` are kept on save, never dropped.\n- The pane's `scan_dir` hook lists the user folder.\n\nEditing a machine *file* is a save action with its own confirmation, not an undoable project edit (#287 rules).\n\n**Done means:** app tests for the read, edit, validate and write round-trip (unknown keys kept, a refused file not written), and a UI test that creates a machine from a template, changes its travels and coolant/live-tool codes, and saves it.\n",
